From: MidnightRAT <midnight@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] deps: build Blosc as C99 explicitly

Blosc's CMakeLists.txt only appends -std=gnu99 for i386/i686/x86_64/amd64.
On aarch64 no -std flag is passed, so GCC 16 falls back to its default
(gnu23), where "bool" is a keyword and blosc/shuffle.c:25
"typedef _Bool bool;" becomes a hard error.

Force the C standard through CMake's own mechanism instead of touching the
architecture list: CMAKE_C_STANDARD=99 + CMAKE_C_EXTENSIONS=ON makes CMake
pass -std=gnu99 on every architecture.  On x86_64 this is a redundant
duplicate of the flag Blosc already adds, so behavior there is unchanged.

---
 deps/Blosc/Blosc.cmake | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/deps/Blosc/Blosc.cmake
+++ b/deps/Blosc/Blosc.cmake
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@
             -DPREFER_EXTERNAL_ZLIB=ON
             -DDEACTIVATE_SSE2=ON
             -DDEACTIVATE_AVX2=ON
+            -DCMAKE_C_STANDARD=99
+            -DCMAKE_C_EXTENSIONS=ON
     )
 else()
     orcaslicer_add_cmake_project(Blosc
@@ -41,6 +43,8 @@
             -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF 
             -DBUILD_BENCHMARKS=OFF 
             -DPREFER_EXTERNAL_ZLIB=ON
+            -DCMAKE_C_STANDARD=99
+            -DCMAKE_C_EXTENSIONS=ON
     )
 endif()
 if (MSVC)
